{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, beating RNA-only multiprofile avgpool (0.591) by ~3 points, confirming that adding image with concat fusion provides a modest gain. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Uncertainty: We do not know whether the fusion mechanism matters—weighted fusion could allow the model to better calibrate the contribution of the weak image modality (image-only was only 0.208) versus the strong RNA signal. This experiment (config_019) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, holding all other settings identical to config_018. This clean A/B comparison will clarify whether fusion strategy is a meaningful design axis, directly informing whether future multimodal experiments should prioritize concat or weighted fusion. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information single step: it exploits the current best configuration while resolving a key uncertainty that affects all subsequent multimodal choices."
}

